{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-09-28T15:31:49.498Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"cfe1c68832b461d2ff5b10a0","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.283","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-prrlce"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Release runs record no trigger origin: the 04:45 dispatcher is indistinguishable from an operator, its failures fall outside the only reliability measure, and the planned manual same-day exception keys on the same event"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Since pm-9url9h the primary daily release path is a local timer that calls gh workflow run auto-release.yml with push=true, dry_run=false and telemetry_mode=off, which is exactly what an operator re-run sends. All three 2026-09-28 release runs therefore read actor unbraind, event workflow_dispatch: dispatcher run 36371013489 failed at the Sentry gate (PM-CLI-3D, owner pm-z329kd), a later dispatch 36375818142 cut 2026.9.28 but its tag-triggered Release failed Windows npm-global acceptance (owner pm-q7c36n), and Release dispatch 36380136948 published. Which of these was the timer and which a person cannot be recovered from the run record. The rolling reliability measure (release-reliability.mjs) selects event schedule only and its collector does not even list other events (excluded_events is empty in run 36414208743, which reports 0.40 against a 0.10 policy), so the primary path has no attempts, failures or stage breakdown anywhere, and the later scheduled run records a success for a day whose automatic path failed. Separately, open pm-uenmu9 specifies the manual same-day follow-up (YYYY.M.D-N) as an explicit workflow_dispatch; with the dispatcher on the same event, the workflow cannot enforce at most one automatic release per UTC day by itself and relies on the dispatcher's client-side tag check."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:release","automation","diagnostics","horizon:current"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-09-28T15:31:49.498Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-28T15:31:49.498Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":300},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Every Auto Release and Release run carries an explicit trigger origin (native schedule, morning dispatcher, blocker retry, operator) from a declared input and its run name, never inferred from event or actor; Release reliability reports a separate series per origin, including the dispatcher's attempts, failures and failing stages, while the native scheduled denominator stays unchanged as decided on pm-9url9h; The same-day manual follow-up of pm-uenmu9 requires an explicit follow-up request from the operator origin; negative control: a dispatcher-origin run after a same-day tag exists skips before any version mutation; The 2026-09-28 dispatcher failure is visible in the new series or recorded as an explicit pre-attribution gap"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-u9d0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A release run states who asked for it; the automatic primary path has its own measured reliability; only an explicit operator request can mint a same-day follow-up release."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Dispatcher and operator runs are identical in GitHub's record, the dispatcher path is absent from reliability reporting, and the manual-exception design keys on the event both paths share."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"release automation"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-9url9h","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-09-28T15:31:49.498Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-e70zh5","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-09-28T15:31:49.498Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-o0sqz5","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-09-28T15:31:49.498Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"2df400f4cec8a1ac45505e2f090b67e7d4d99658c87e6a09cc0f634cc166e564","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a6f8bd86d8f55efd25b3230b9f73e345e17852de1ecaff01b27b2dd9f28322b3"}
